{
  "abstract": "Zero-Mathlib Lean 4.35.0 formalization resolving two structural questions left open by Vinciguerra's operator analysis of passive-output catalytic register programs (arXiv:2609.18692). The 17 compared theorems prove: (1) an exact base-p digit-sum dichotomy f in RP^{pass}_{F_p}(2, t) iff s_p(d) <= min(p - 1, t - 1) for all d >= 2 with alpha_d != 0, yielding unbounded-degree 2-access Frobenius collapse (x^{p^m}), exact F_2 saturation (x^3 impossible for all t), the impossibility threshold s_p(d) >= p, characteristic-0 recovery for d < p, and a literal commutative-ring soundness bridge; (2) strictly bilinear 2-access Frobenius collapse x^{2^k} in k + 1 registers and 4k - 2 bilinear ops over any characteristic-2 commutative ring; (3) explicit 3-register Pascal-row shear loops computing x^7, x^9, x^11, x^13, and x^15 in 5..9 accesses, unconditional global integer optimality of log_13 8 < 30/37 < log_{2t-3} t for all t >= 4 (t != 8), complete 4-register passive powering for every N >= 1 in < (104/3) * 8^ell accesses, and pointwise product-ring streaming frequency moments F_D over R^n; and (4) a balanced zero-workspace bilinear multilinear product x_0...x_{2^k - 1} with every operation explicitly constrained by CatOp.usesOnly to at most k + 2 designated registers and exact primitive op count (7 * (2^k)^2 - 4) / 3.",
